WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Imagine if we could go back in time.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.000
Imagine if we could see what our ocean looked like

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.500
in a world with less human impact.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Marine Protected Areas offer us a glimpse of this dream.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Only 5,000 in number,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.500
they are the nature reserves of the sea.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:49.000
Countries have agreed that 10% of marine and coastal areas must be protected by 2020. 

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
But today only 1 in 10 countries protect more than 2% of their marine areas.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.800
Marine Protected Areas, like nature reserves on land,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.000
nurture recovery and bring new economic opportunities.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Yet, most existing marine parks and reserves are vastly under-funded.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.500
Without effective stewardship, surveillance and accountability,

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.000
marine protected areas fail to provide the safe sanctuaries they promise to deliver.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.500
The risks run higher in developing countries and traditional coastal communities,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.500
where inhabitants stand to lose the marine resources they depend on.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:53.500
How can we, together, ensure that 10% of our ocean will be efficiently protected by 2020? 

